# Phase-1.1 feedback polish, joined: HQ pick -> positional key -> menu ->
# settings slider -> grid toggle -> scroll -> fixed Back -> Close Menu.
# Frames are 1-based. Coordinates are screen pixels at the starting camera.
#
# Deliberately *focused*, next to `rts_acceptance_v1.script` rather than folded
# into it: the canonical run owns the economy loop and its audio counters are
# pinned cue by cue, so adding this chrome to it would only inflate those
# numbers. Nothing here issues a unit order, so every voice counter of this
# run stays 0 and the whole exit line is about the feedback surface.
#
# Every coordinate below is a centre (or the start) of an exported rect, never
# a hand-measured pixel — `the_focused_script_coordinates_hit_what_they_name`
# in `crates/mmd-engine/tests/rts_acceptance.rs` re-derives each one from the
# live layout/hit tests and fails if a rect ever moves.

1:move:960,518
4:lclick:960,518               # the HQ's own footprint corner (160.5,160.5): a Pick::Building
8:key:q                        # positional slot 0 = Worker; the HQ is selected, so it is enabled

16:lclick:1888,24              # MENU_RECT centre -> paused menu
24:lclick:960,540              # PAUSE_MENU_SETTINGS_BTN centre -> settings panel

32:drag:568,288,1170,288       # keyboard-pan track, left edge -> the 78 cells/s step
40:lclick:960,580              # GRID_CONTROL_RECT centre [568,564,784,32] -> show_grid = false
48:wheel:960,540,-1            # inside SETTINGS_BODY_VIEWPORT: one notch down, +72 px
56:lclick:552,928              # SETTINGS_BACK_BTN centre — fixed footer, unmoved by the scroll
64:lclick:960,620              # PAUSE_MENU_CLOSE_BTN centre -> gameplay

72:quit
